A||||4||billfredmike24||Driver side door lock||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||06-06-2000||07:32 PM||||I can't lock or unlock the drivers side from the outside with the keys.  I've yet to take the door panel off, but from reading other posts i figure it's the U shaped part that i need.  Does anyone know where i can get one and how much it will cost<BR>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-07-2000||09:49 AM||||You'll  have to be a little more specific. If you can lock/unlock the door from the inside, then the lock cylinder or it's linkage has to be the problem.  They're fairly easy to change.  Pull the inner door panel off.  There's one big access hole towards the rear of the door.  There's a support beam that runs across it.  Do yourself a favor and drill out the rivets.  (I replaced the rivets with short bolts.)  <P>This is gonna take 4 pages to explain (I'm tired---What's new).  Let me see if I still have some pics that should explain it better.<P>This one might help.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/doorhandleassy_1.JPG"> <BR>Crappy pic.  Sorry.  You can see the part that's attached to the cylinder.  Attached to that is the linkage that should run towards the rear of the door.  You can barely see the (to the left of the cyl) a little black piece.  That's part of the "U" shaped clip that holds the cyl in place.  Sometimes that's a real B**** to get loose.  Don't drop it.  It's even worse to get to it once it's fallen.  Pull/pry that out and the cyl will pull right out of the door (towards the inside).  Remove the linkage and replace it.  Piece of cake (usually).  If you have any questions, feel free to email me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||blayde8||06-08-2000||03:27 AM||||Same thing happened to me.  I can't unlock or lock the drivers side door from the outside with the key.  I have no idea what the problem is, but right now, that's the last thing I need to fix as I can just unlock it from the passenger side.  Now to change the master brake cylinder....then I can't forget to bleed those brakes... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  ||||reg||13
Z||000003||billfredmike24||06-08-2000||01:30 PM||||I fixed it, but it might not be a good idea.  I took the panel off and looked inside and the problem was that as the key was turning, it wasnt catching the washer shaped part, it looked like it was stripped.<BR>i wasnt sure if i could get to it or if i could get the part to fix it, so i used some silicone so it wasnt slipping.  All i can say is i can now use my keys.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-08-2000||05:59 PM||||The small washer shaped part is just a retainer and has a small, integral clip that keeps it on the cylinder.  If you're referring to the larger part that the linkage connects to, that's supposed to move.  That way you can unlock the door from the inside without breaking the lock cylinder.  Just some friendly advice from someone who's been there more than once. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
